1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,165
Most pages need more than text.

2
00:00:03,165 --> 00:00:07,552
A Media Field attaches images and other files to a content item, from

3
00:00:07,552 --> 00:00:09,717
the media library or by upload.

4
00:00:09,717 --> 00:00:13,870
This video shows how to add the field, choose files, and pick one

5
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:15,450
of its three editors.

6
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:24,733
A Media Field stores the location of each file, not the file itself.

7
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:30,365
Usually the file lives in the media library, so one image can appear on many pages.

8
00:00:30,365 --> 00:00:35,870
Each file can carry a description, the media text, and a focal point, the anchor.

9
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,644
The field has three editors.

10
00:00:38,644 --> 00:00:43,227
Standard opens the media library in a dialog, where you pick files, and

11
00:00:43,227 --> 00:00:46,619
Gallery shows the same files as cards or as a list.

12
00:00:46,619 --> 00:00:50,250
Attached uploads files that belong to the content item.

13
00:00:54,477 --> 00:00:56,655
Fields belong to content types.

14
00:00:56,655 --> 00:01:01,777
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, you find every type of the site.

15
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:04,724
Open the Page type with its Edit button.

16
00:01:04,724 --> 00:01:08,939
The Fields section lists the fields of the type, and Add Field adds one.

17
00:01:09,396 --> 00:01:14,981
Enter Photos as the Display Name, and the Technical Name fills in by itself.

18
00:01:14,981 --> 00:01:19,476
Choose Media Field as the Field Type, then Save & Configure.

19
00:01:23,682 --> 00:01:26,591
The settings decide how the field behaves.

20
00:01:26,591 --> 00:01:32,468
Required forces editors to choose at least one file, and Multiple lets them choose several.

21
00:01:32,468 --> 00:01:36,952
The Hint is a line of help shown above the field, so let's type one.

22
00:01:37,403 --> 00:01:42,271
Allow media text lets editors describe each file, and it is on by default.

23
00:01:42,271 --> 00:01:45,982
Allow anchors lets them mark a focal point on an image.

24
00:01:45,982 --> 00:01:48,903
It is off by default, so let's turn it on.

25
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:54,339
By default the field accepts every type of file that the media library accepts.

26
00:01:54,339 --> 00:01:58,960
Clear Allow all default media types to choose the types yourself, such as

27
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,587
image types, and the dialog then lists only those files.

28
00:02:03,043 --> 00:02:06,960
Further down, the question What type of editor should be used?

29
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,495
offers Standard, Gallery and Attached.

30
00:02:09,495 --> 00:02:11,973
Let's keep Standard, and choose Save.

31
00:02:16,183 --> 00:02:18,477
To use the field, create a Page.

32
00:02:18,477 --> 00:02:23,306
Under Content, Content Items, the New menu lists the types you can create.

33
00:02:23,306 --> 00:02:24,393
Choose Page.

34
00:02:24,855 --> 00:02:26,056
Enter a Title.

35
00:02:26,056 --> 00:02:30,922
The Photos field shows its Hint, and No Files, because nothing is attached.

36
00:02:30,922 --> 00:02:33,685
Add media opens the Select Media dialog.

37
00:02:34,148 --> 00:02:37,061
The dialog is the media library itself.

38
00:02:37,061 --> 00:02:41,916
Open a folder, search, or upload files, then tick the files you want.

39
00:02:41,916 --> 00:02:46,578
Only image files are listed, because the field allows image types.

40
00:02:47,030 --> 00:02:49,614
The footer counts the selected files.

41
00:02:49,614 --> 00:02:54,660
OK adds them to the field, and each file appears as a thumbnail with its name.

42
00:02:55,112 --> 00:02:57,485
Click a thumbnail to select it.

43
00:02:57,485 --> 00:03:01,334
The toolbar then shows Remove, Media text, and Anchor.

44
00:03:01,334 --> 00:03:07,042
Media text opens a box where you describe the image for visitors who cannot see it.

45
00:03:07,493 --> 00:03:11,340
In the Enter media text box, type a description of the image, such

46
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:13,423
as Spring orchard, and choose OK.

47
00:03:13,877 --> 00:03:16,110
Anchor opens a box with the image.

48
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:20,017
Click the point that must stay in view when a template crops the

49
00:03:20,017 --> 00:03:21,691
picture, then choose OK.

50
00:03:21,691 --> 00:03:24,537
Reset Anchor returns the point to the center.

51
00:03:24,994 --> 00:03:26,116
Choose Publish.

52
00:03:26,116 --> 00:03:29,214
A message confirms that the Page has been published.

53
00:03:29,674 --> 00:03:31,705
Let's open the page on the site.

54
00:03:31,705 --> 00:03:35,392
It shows the images, and the media text of an image becomes its

55
00:03:35,392 --> 00:03:38,384
alternative text, which screen readers read aloud.

56
00:03:42,567 --> 00:03:46,627
The editor is a setting of the field, so you can change it later.

57
00:03:46,627 --> 00:03:51,372
In the settings of Photos, choose Gallery from the list of editors, and Save.

58
00:03:51,372 --> 00:03:56,747
The chosen files stay in place, because both editors keep a list of media library files.

59
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,113
Let's edit the Page again.

60
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:03,416
The Gallery editor shows each file as a card, with buttons for its

61
00:04:03,416 --> 00:04:06,226
media text, anchor, download and removal.

62
00:04:06,226 --> 00:04:10,470
The Add media card at the end opens the same Select Media dialog.

63
00:04:10,921 --> 00:04:13,738
The toolbar switches between cards and a list.

64
00:04:13,738 --> 00:04:17,422
Drag a card onto another to change the order of the files, and

65
00:04:17,422 --> 00:04:19,101
Publish keeps that order.

66
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:27,228
The Attached editor suits a file that belongs to one page.

67
00:04:27,228 --> 00:04:31,831
Let's add a second Media Field to the Page type, named Visitor Guide,

68
00:04:31,831 --> 00:04:33,550
with Save & Configure.

69
00:04:34,032 --> 00:04:38,101
The guide is one PDF, so in the settings clear Multiple.

70
00:04:38,101 --> 00:04:42,958
Clear Allow all default media types, tick .pdf in the list of types,

71
00:04:42,958 --> 00:04:45,583
and choose Attached as the editor.

72
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:47,092
Then choose Save.

73
00:04:47,547 --> 00:04:51,527
When you edit the Page, Visitor Guide has an Add media button that

74
00:04:51,527 --> 00:04:56,170
uploads a file from your computer, instead of opening the Select Media dialog.

75
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:58,657
The uploaded file appears in the field.

76
00:04:59,108 --> 00:05:03,448
When the page is saved, here with Publish, the uploaded file moves from

77
00:05:03,448 --> 00:05:07,168
a temporary location into a folder that belongs to the page.

78
00:05:07,628 --> 00:05:11,199
On the site, a file that is not an image appears as a link.

79
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:14,605
The link text is the media text, or the path of the file

80
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:15,978
when there is none.

81
00:05:17,578 --> 00:05:20,836
Deleting the page deletes the files in its folder.

82
00:05:20,836 --> 00:05:27,758
Using the Attached editor requires the Manage Attached Media Fields Folder permission, which administrators have.

83
00:05:29,758 --> 00:05:31,312
That is the Media Field:

84
00:05:31,312 --> 00:05:34,989
files from the library or uploaded to the page, each with its own

85
00:05:34,989 --> 00:05:38,252
description, in the editor that fits how your team works.

86
00:05:38,252 --> 00:05:39,598
Thanks for watching.

